# Der Koloss — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` for local tooling if you need it. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The game needs NO environment variables and NO secrets. It is a static site
# with no build step: serve this directory over any local web server and it
# runs. Nothing below is read at runtime by the game.
#
# There are no API keys, no accounts, and no analytics in this directory. The
# only network calls the client makes are for its own assets and for peer-to-peer
# co-op.
#
# Co-op signaling, STUN and TURN come from the Rainfine Game Hall deployment, not
# from a public broker: the page reads `/api/runtime-config` (Cloudflare Pages
# Function) and then `<WEBRTC_SERVICE_URL>/rtc-config`. Nothing in this directory
# hardcodes a hostname, and there is deliberately no fallback to the public
# PeerJS broker — if the hall has no WebRTC service configured, co-op reports
# "联机服务未配置" instead of silently working over a third-party server.
#
# To run co-op against a local gateway without touching the source, set
# `window.YUQING_WEBRTC_SERVICE_URL = "http://127.0.0.1:9000"` before the game
# scripts load, or open the page with `?webrtc=http://127.0.0.1:9000`.

# Canonical domain for share/invite links if you deploy your own copy.
# Consumed by deploy tooling only — never by the game.
# SITE_URL=https://example.com
